<!--
  Volume panel background: flat black, square.

  Target definition (packages/SystemUI/res/drawable/volume_dialog_background.xml
  at lineage-23.2, lines 17-22):

      <shape android:shape="rectangle">
          <corners android:radius="@dimen/volume_dialog_background_corner_radius"/>
          <solid android:color="@androidprv:color/materialColorSurface" />
      </shape>

  Live shipped APK (aapt2 dump xmltree /tmp/sysui.apk): corners = @dimen/…
  (30 dp) and solid = 0x010602d3 = @androidprv:color/materialColorSurface.
  The consistent black is token color.chrome.action_centre #000000
  (ztmetro.c:6501-6502); radius 0 is token metrics.corner_radius_dp 0
  (ztmetro.c:3657-3697).

  Inline literals only: idmap2 maps this file by (type,name) and the target
  AssetManager must not need a cross-package reference.  The Compose content
  inside the panel (slider, labels) is NOT affected by this drawable — see
  evidence/volume-power-toast/REPORT.md §4.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">
    <corners android:radius="0dp" />
    <solid android:color="#FF000000" />
</shape>
